    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14903" root="رجع" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَاجِعَةٌ</span></b>  [originally fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَاجِعٌ</span>, q. v.]: see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجِيعَةٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجْعٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also, [app. from the
returning of its water time after time,] (assumed tropical:)  <i>A water-course of a valley.</i> (ISh, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَوَاجِعُ</span> [is its
pl., and] signifies <i>Varying winds;</i> because of
their coming and going. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  Hence also,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَوَاجِعُ الأَبْوَابِ</span> [<i>The leaves of doors</i>]. (TA.)

